From: opencode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:35:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH] [Quantization] Support native Quark W4A16 INT4/UINT4
 exports (#48606)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Version-locked to VLLM_REF=v0.30.0 (rebased 2026-09-22; git apply
--check clean on the v0.30.0 tag). Upstream PR #48606 MERGED to main
2026-09-18 (6df2b1a8), AFTER the v0.30.0 branch cut — verified NOT in
the v0.30.0 tag. Drop when a pinned VLLM_REF contains the merge, and
confirm ROCm/gfx1201 kernel coverage, not just the merge: the dense
QuarkW4A16Int4 path selects an MPLinearKernel at load time (ROCm order:
RDNA3/gfx1100-only, then RDNAHybrid gfx11/gfx12, then TritonW4A16
fallback), so gfx1201 support is proven only by the AWQ trial boot.

v0.30.0 rebase: v0.30.0 already uses the PR's post-review structure
(_get_scheme_cls_from_config returning key tuples + init_scheme, MoE
detector returning (keys, method_cls)), so this rebase mirrors the
MERGED upstream version instead of the v0.29.0 adaptation:
- quark.py: QuantKeyMatch _is_w4a16_int4, key-tuple dispatch branch,
  init_scheme weight_config path + W4A16 construction, layer_name=prefix
  at the get_moe_method call site. The v0.29.0 backport's duplicate
  _unwrap_single_quant_config is dropped (native in v0.30.0).
- quark_moe.py: key-tuple detector branch, layer_name param + W4A16
  branch in get_moe_method, MoE method __init__ takes quant keys and
  calls super().__init__(moe, keys) like upstream.
- schemes/quark_w4a16_int4.py: super().__init__ restored (v0.30.0
  QuarkScheme has __init__); has_g_idx dropped (removed upstream by
  #54809); symmetry/group handling identical to merged upstream.
- utils.py: parse/canonicalize helpers unchanged from merged upstream.
- Unchanged carriers: mp-linear log line, triton_moe kInt4StaticAsym
  order, auto_awq symmetric (w_zp_name None) support.
NOTE to future editors: this file is applied with git apply, which
silently truncates a hunk body that exceeds its @@ line count — always
regenerate via git diff/format-patch instead of hand-editing counts.
